        "notes": "VERIFIED: Cayley-Hamilton for 2x2 is B^2 = tr(B)B - det(B)1; a 2-dimensional space carrying a preserved non-degenerate alternating form gives B in Sp(2) = SL_2 hence det B = 1; B^{n+2} = B^n(tau B - 1) = tau B^{n+1} - B^n; and tau = (a^(n) + a^(n+2))/a^(n+1) inverts the recurrence correctly. The standard facts invoked are also right \u2014 the cup-product pairing is topological hence flat for the Gauss-Manin connection, and Hodge-Riemann makes the (1,0)-(0,1) pairing perfect for a curve. The one asserted step is that the S_5-invariant form restricts NON-DEGENERATELY to the rank-2 W-isotypic plane, which is plausible for a self-dual W but is stated rather than shown. The parent block's superseded 'last open number' claim does not appear here."
